# Coding-agent local notes (contain secrets — never commit)

# Generated by the release workflow
RELEASE_NOTES.md

# Local session docs (never committed)
docs/*

# ...except the durable architecture notes, which belong in the repo
!docs/WORKSPACE.md
!docs/PRIVATELM_REFERENCE.md
!docs/MODELS.md
!docs/SHIZUKU.md
!docs/superpowers/

# Two that were missing from the list above, and the rule that decided it:
# **if `AGENTS.md` tells the reader to open a file before touching something, that
# file has to be in the repo.** Otherwise the instruction points at a path that
# only exists on the machine of whoever wrote it.
#
# `HYBRID_CORE.md` is the one that was actually missing, and it is the doc this
# guide calls mandatory before anything that depends on the Rust core — including
# the reason the branch must not be deleted. `HANDOFF.md` is the datad snapshot
# that says what is measured, what is not, and what the next step is; the next
# session needs it to be in the repo for the same reason, and not in a
# conversation that ends with the harness.
!docs/HYBRID_CORE.md
!docs/HANDOFF.md

# Stale entries from the parked Rust core (`mobilelm_core`, removed in 0.3.5 — see
# docs/HYBRID_CORE.md). Nothing produces these two files any more; CI no longer
# copies them into jniLibs, and `release.yml` warns if `liblitert-lm.so` reappears
# in an APK.
#
# They stay listed anyway, as a net: the cdylib is 436 KB and the C API runtime
# 37,2 MB, a developer with an old worktree still has them on disk, and
# `jniLibs/arm64-v8a/` is exactly where a stray `flutter build` would pick them up.
# Ignoring by name is deliberate — `libomp.so` sits in that same directory and is
# committed on purpose, so ignoring the directory would silently untrack it.
/android/app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libmobilelm_core.so
/android/app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/liblitert-lm.so
